<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 471)</h2>
<p><b>You decide when the originals come out.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>⌥R — Show Original Frame.</b> Pulls the real frame behind an optimized stand-in whenever you want it, and again to go back, so it doubles as an A/B. Pausing no longer does this on its own: a pause isn't the same as asking to inspect, and fetching a full-res frame every time you stop re-incurs the cost the stand-in exists to avoid. There's a setting if you do want it on every pause.</li>
<li><b>Zooming past 1:1 or opening the scopes still fetches the original automatically</b> — those are you asking to interrogate the image.</li>
<li><b>Press play while zoomed in and Asobi asks, once, which you want</b>: the stand-in playing smoothly, or the original frames at full detail. It remembers, and you can change it in Settings.</li>
<li>Playback itself always uses the stand-in unless you've said otherwise, whatever the zoom.</li>
<li>Spelling throughout the app is now US English.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
